      "id": 149329,
      "name": "bluedarky",
      "username": "bluedarky",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-10-09T20:49:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"waedens\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/w/b3f665/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> waedens:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would expect the lag to increase a little bit with each expansion as each one introduces new mechanisms and twists that they need to cross check against the old content. Obviously even if there weren't new game mechanics the play testing of every combination of heroes because increasingly complex. I could be completely wrong though as I am not in the business and there may be tools and short cuts I don't know or understand.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In part, what's been done before helps, probably the most complicated elements will be Miss Information's front side not being a target, Abandoned Hero, and Unforgiving Wasteland as most of the other things in the decks have already been implimented.</p>\n<p>Conversely Miss Information's front side lays the groundwork for Kaagra Warfang's front side making Wrath arrive a slight bit faster.</p>",
