    {
      "id": 149335,
      "name": "morph147",
      "username": "morph147",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-10-11T01:10:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>based off my extensive programming background and the program's I create, for text only and no pictures or cosmetics, in their toolbox should take 24 hours max to write the code for each deck for how they think it should run. Then 2 weeks of play testing that deck repeatedly in combos of every deck played at least 3 times with as much of all the cards playing as possible. During those two weeks the cosmetic stuff can be added in. Then once all decks are hopefully programmed, another 2 weeks of testing along with any new features they want to add. From there it's a submission to Apple to wait two more weeks and some more play testing. So depending on how many people they have building the decks and play testing an individual deck speeds up what is going on.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Therefore since I am hoping they have made the decks while testing multiplayer, and there is only 3 in the pack, I am guessing we should see our first demo deck on the stream this Tuesday, this coming weekend if they do any special streams for the anniversary, or the following Tuesday. Then based off a complex algorithm of release dates based off past ones called MigrantP is secretly stalking me and sets up releases the week after I go on a trip and have a bunch of downtime to play.... It will come out the last week in November or beginning of December.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>p.s. Kidding on MigrantP stalking me but not about them releasing it the week after I get back from downtime trips.</p>",
